    "text": {
     "en": "Spectacles are glasses worn to see better. 'Pair' means two things that go together, such as a pair of spectacles or shoes.\n'Glanced' means took a quick look. 'Searching' means looking carefully for something.\nUse each word in a sentence of your own, for example: I glanced at the clock.\nThe word 'pair' appears in phrases like a pair of shoes, and it is often confused in sound with 'peer'.\nCircle the correct spelling in lists such as water, vegetables, balloon, house, elephant, spectacles, carpenter, fruit, receive and principal.\nNote the opposites in the crossword: far and near, slow and fast, hot and cold.\n(additional, not in the textbook) Keep a word notebook and add three new words from each lesson."
    }
